y  occupation or a situation required by  the security realities in the area or  somewhere in between right that's a very  legitimate and important conversation to  have the idea that Israel's mere  creation is the occupation is laughably  out of this world and I would love to  talk to some of these women's studies  individuals who pass this resolution or  people from the Portland State  University State Senate that passed this  resolution it's like they think one day  israel appeared and confiscated  sovereign Palestinian land and I've said  this before and it bears repeating  countries are created one of three ways  on this planet this applies to all  countries one annexation or purchased  that's one way in which countries are  created to war or invasion or takeover  and three international treaty Israel  was created by international treaty its  existence is no more or less legitimate  than the existence of any other country  if you are going to not do business with  companies that do business with Israel  based on Israel being an occupying force  not because of what's going on now in  Gaza and the West Bank but from its mere  creation in 1948 you should not be doing  business with any American company  whatsoever  because by that same logic this entire  thing we call the United States of  America most of it and and the part that  was purchased was purchased at a  pittance pittance from pittance that's a  kind of difficult word to say for a very  small amount of money a total ripoff  right from from natives that were here  before Europeans came and you could  argue that it is just as much of an  occupation as what's going on in Israel  but I want to go further right because  there's a lot of people who don't even  realize that Israel was not created from  land that wasn't previously some  Palestinian country this goes back to  understanding the history of the British  Empire controlling the land and this  goes back even further to the Ottoman  Empire it involves J